{#
	A table's column heading, a link that sorts the list by it when it can (sh: key, label, href, sortable, active,
	direction, width, wide; sort_region and sort_results: the list's region and results, swapped by htmx). The attributes
	are written as literal markup with only their values interpolated: built as a string by an expression, Twig would
	escape the quotes and the browser would receive the width as text.

	sh.end (optional) puts the heading at the column's end, over numbers set right.

	sh.wide marks a column a phone does not show (data-phone="hide"): Core hides the whole column
	at 700px and narrower, and the row's tooltip still shows its value.
#}
{% if sh.sortable %}
	<th class="sortable-header {{ sh.active ? 'is-sorted' : '' }}{{ sh.end|default(false) ? ' text-end' : '' }}"
	    {% if sh.width %}style="width:{{ sh.width }}%"{% endif %}
	    {% if sh.wide|default(false) %}data-phone="hide"{% endif %}
	    {% if sh.active %}aria-sort="{{ sh.direction == 'desc' ? 'descending' : 'ascending' }}"{% endif %}>
		<a href="{{ sh.href }}"
			   hx-get="{{ sh.href }}" hx-target="#{{ sort_region }}" hx-select="#{{ sort_results }}"
			   hx-swap="innerHTML" hx-push-url="true" hx-indicator="closest .cl-ui-table">
		{{ sh.label }}<span class="sortable-indicator" aria-hidden="true">{{ sh.active ? (sh.direction == 'desc' ? '▼' : '▲') : '↕' }}</span>
		</a>
	</th>
{% else %}
	<th{% if sh.end|default(false) %} class="text-end"{% endif %} {% if sh.width %}style="width:{{ sh.width }}%"{% endif %} {% if sh.wide|default(false) %}data-phone="hide"{% endif %}>
		{{ sh.label }}
	</th>
{% endif %}
